# Environments
# Anchored with a leading slash: these name virtualenvs at the repo root.
# Unanchored, `env/` matches a directory called `env` at *any* depth, which
# swallowed deploy/env/ and every template inside it — and git does not
# descend into an ignored directory, so no negation could rescue them.
.env
.venv
/env/
/venv/
/ENV/
/env.bak/
/venv.bak/
/my_env

# mkdocs documentation 
/site 

